## Compatibility changes

Pinned `MQClientAPIImpl.getBrokerHAStatus(String,long)` now maps to
`MQClientApi::get_broker_ha_status` for request 907. Rust sends no header or
request body, uses the supplied Broker address without VIP conversion, and
preserves the caller timeout. New `HaRuntimeInfo` and nested connection/client
DTOs match Java primitive defaults, nullable nested fields, list/object
initializers, mutable shared references, and Fastjson field names. The invoked
Java fixture and Rust loopback test cover populated/default bodies, a success
without a body, a Broker error, and exact request-envelope behavior.

The full local Rust run also exposed stale fixture-count assertions. The tests
now expect six broker-maintenance cases, five topic-list cases, and 44 request
header identity entries; the correction-header Java alias is mapped explicitly.
The direct API audit has three of its initial 18 candidates closed and 15 open.

## Evidence still open

The wider P18-V01 settings, inputs, errors, control flows and reverse-export
audit remains open. Current-revision GitHub Ubuntu/native-Windows P18-V04
results are unavailable under the no-remote-CI constraint. No Docker or Broker
was used. The four pre-existing Phase 19 worktree paths remain untouched and
unstaged.

Log correction: the whitespace check command was `git diff --check` (not
`cargo diff --check`); it passed.
